{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/73907-earthbound","id":73907,"title":"Earthbound","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-17T15:14:42-08:00","id":73907,"title":"Earthbound","content":"I don't know how many people are familiar with the Earthbound from oWoD Demon, but I always thought they were wonderful antagonists who would work well in Vigil. In particular, I thought it would be cool to have them be an enemy for the Lucifuge in particular, recruiting their errant descendents. Any thoughts on these bad guys?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-18T06:16:01-08:00","id":74226,"title":"","content":"I've used them as antagonists in Vampire the Requiem games. They have a nice mix of power and corruption that makes them and their minions good foils for vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T17:05:11-07:00","id":165380,"title":"","content":"I loved using the Earthbound and their cults as antagonists in Hunter the Reckoning games. I think they could work well for Vigil Hunters as well, though it might be best if you focused on the cult itself. Depending on the power scale you are using, only the weakest Earthbound demons would be able to be destroyed by a group of Hunters, Lucifuge or not. The Lucifuge would have a distinct advantage, though. Since the demons of the Old and New World of Darkness are so different, how would you reconcile the Abyss?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If people were meant to run around naked, they would be born that way.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1286-nikuchan","name":"Nikuchan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1286_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T17:30:13-07:00","id":165423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Instead of inhabiting human hosts, they reside in inanimate objects known as <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Reliquary_%28DTF%29\" target=\"_blank\">reliquaries</a>, either because they are too powerful for a human body to endure their presence, because they were summoned and bound into such an object, or because there simply was no suitable new human host around when they lost their old hosts. </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=U6kp4zBF-Rc\" data-code=\"U6kp4zBF-Rc\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/U6kp4zBF-Rc/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T05:19:10-07:00","id":165819,"title":"","content":"I LOVE Earthbound. I LOVE cWoD Demon.<br /> <br /> Could easily just make them really powerful spirits that are bound within a physical object (or a plant, like Avitu and the tree), if for whatever reason you didn't want to &quot;violate&quot; nWoD fluff. Though I've NO idea where nWoD is on God/Angels/Fallen Angels, other than that Infernal mentions something along the lines of &quot;they might maybe be biblical demons&quot;, and there's the God-Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T14:49:48-07:00","id":200415,"title":"","content":"The idea of a Earthbound is that they are to alien for the human body to hold to massive in nature or ideas so i must ask can a Dragon Be an earthbound?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3507-hollow_fang","name":"Hollow_Fang","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[